Why This Matters
Mutual TLS is a critical security feature that provides:

Authentication: Both client and server verify each other's identity
Encryption: All communication is encrypted in transit
Integrity: Data cannot be tampered with during transmission
Zero Trust Architecture: No implicit trust between services
Key Takeaways
mTLS provides end-to-end security for service-to-service communication in microservices architectures
Istio simplifies mTLS implementation by handling certificate management and policy enforcement automatically
Gradual rollout strategies help minimize disruption when implementing mTLS in existing systems
Monitoring and observability are essential for maintaining healthy mTLS implementations
Performance considerations must be balanced against security requirements
